# Atlas Delta Deployment Strategy Analysis

**Project:** Atlas Delta  
**Service:** Real-time Anomaly Scoring API  
**Traffic Target:** 12k req/s, p95 under 120ms  
**Marker:** ATLAS-DELTA-77

---

## 1. Three Approaches

### 1.1 Blue-Green Rollout
Blue-green deployment maintains two identical production environments. Traffic is switched entirely from the "blue" (current) environment to the "green" (new) environment using a load balancer or DNS change. This approach provides instant rollback capability by simply switching traffic back.

### 1.2 Canary with Automated Rollback
Canary deployment gradually routes a small percentage of traffic to the new version while keeping most traffic on the stable version. Automated rollback triggers based on predefined metrics (error rate, latency thresholds). Traffic percentage increases incrementally if health checks pass.

### 1.3 Shadow Deployment with Offline Comparison
